{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" turns persistence into a declare-and-register concern. You annotate a domain entity with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":"; the macro generates its SwiftData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" “shadow” class, the value↔model converters, and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistableEntity"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityDB"},{"text":" actor and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator"},{"text":" build the container, synthesize one ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per registered "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"text":", and reuse the core ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" for debounced, batched writes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate plain value-type entities inside an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"text":"; the plugin observes the changelog and writes through to SwiftData after a debounce. Reads happen once, at launch, into memory — the in-memory ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is the source of truth.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For low-level manual wiring (writing your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"text":"), see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"text":". For the macro details, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"},{"text":". To add cross-device iCloud sync on top, see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Before-you-start","text":"Before you start","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes a Swidux app already exists — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are wired and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If not, follow ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a local-only persistence layer. It needs "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no iCloud, CloudKit, or Push entitlements","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — only the sandbox ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.apple.security.network.client","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entitlement if your app also makes network calls (killswitch, analytics, feature flags). Adding sync entitlements to a local-only app is dead configuration and an App Review risk.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPersistence\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Step-2-Annotate-your-domain-entity-with-Persisted","text":"Step 2: Annotate your domain entity with `@Persisted`","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A persisted entity is a value type that already satisfies "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"ID == UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" contract). Add ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","    var createdAt: Date","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This generates a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CardModel: @Model"},{"text":" class with ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"toDomain()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(from:)"},{"text":", plus ","type":"text"},{"code":"extension Card: PersistableEntity { typealias Model = CardModel }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". By default every stored property is mirrored directly onto the model — SwiftData persists scalars "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" composites natively, so no manual blob columns are needed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated model is "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CloudKit-safe by construction"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" model backs both the local and the synced container (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). SwiftData’s CloudKit mirroring requires every non-optional attribute to be optional or carry a default value, and every relationship to be optional — validated when the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ModelContainer"},{"type":"text","text":" is created. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" satisfies this automatically:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-optional mirrored attributes get a default."}]},{"text":" If you wrote one on the domain property (","type":"text"},{"code":"var count: Int = 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), it is propagated verbatim; otherwise the macro fills a canonical default for the known SwiftData primitives (","type":"text"},{"code":"String → \"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bool → false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", integers\/floats ","type":"text"},{"code":"→ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date → .distantPast","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data → Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"UUID → UUID()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Defaults are inert locally — ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overwrites them on every load.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-primitive, non-optional properties"}]},{"text":" (a custom ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" type, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URL"},{"text":", an enum) have no default the macro can invent. Give the property a default (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"= …"},{"text":"), make it optional, or mark it ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"text":" — otherwise ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" emits a compile-time error.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Relationships are generated optional","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var tags: [TagModel]? = nil"},{"text":"); a non-optional to-one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation"},{"text":" is a compile-time error (CloudKit forbids non-optional relationships).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" blob columns","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" default to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data()"},{"type":"text","text":", so any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type is CloudKit-safe through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":". Because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data()"},{"type":"text","text":" is never decodable, a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"non-optional","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":" property must also carry a domain default ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"= …"},{"type":"text","text":") — the generated getter falls back to it when the blob is missing or undecodable (e.g. a row CloudKit materialized before the blob synced). Omitting the default is a compile-time error ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inlineRequiresDefault"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"entity","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state containers"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" slices). They are different layers and never apply to the same type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Marker macros for non-trivial properties","level":3,"anchor":"Marker-macros-for-non-trivial-properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro can’t infer relationships, foreign keys, or which fields are derived. Four property markers (named to avoid SwiftData’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relationship"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Transient"},{"text":") tell ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" what to do:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","","    @Inline var styling: TextStyling = TextStyling()  \/\/ one opaque JSON Data column","    @ForeignKey var deckID: UUID                      \/\/ scalar parent reference","    @Relation(deleteRule: .cascade, inverse: \\TagModel.card)","    var tags: [Tag]                                   \/\/ SwiftData relationship","    @Ignored var renderedPreview: String?             \/\/ derived; omitted from the model","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Marker"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effect"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(none)"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mirror the property directly (SwiftData persists scalars and "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" composites)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Force a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value into a single JSON ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" column (keeps a CloudKit record compact; sidesteps SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-attribute edge cases).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ForeignKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intent marker on a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID"},{"type":"text","text":"; functionally a mirrored scalar column."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation(deleteRule:inverse:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A SwiftData relationship to another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" entity. The property’s type references the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain"}]},{"type":"text","text":" type ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Tag]"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tag?"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tag"},{"text":"); the model substitutes the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"…Model"},{"text":" shadow. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inverse"},{"text":" is a key path on the generated model, e.g. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\TagModel.card"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleteRule"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxDeleteRule"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cascade"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".nullify"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".noAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Ignored"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exclude a derived\/denormalized property. Must be optional so it can be reconstructed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" on load."}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" does not generate an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Attribute(.unique)"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" — CloudKit forbids unique constraints — so the same generated model works for both local and synced containers. The cost is that rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" are possible. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":" handles them by converging rather than by assuming uniqueness: writes update every matching row, deletions remove every matching row, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetchAll"},{"type":"text","text":" collapses to one value per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":". Nothing deletes a duplicate as a side effect of a write."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note","style":"note"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 3: Put the `EntityStore` on your state","anchor":"Step-3-Put-the-EntityStore-on-your-state"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    var cards: EntityStore<Card> = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.cards"},{"type":"text","text":" like any "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.cards[card.id] = card"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.cards.modify(id) { … }"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.cards[id] = nil"},{"type":"text","text":". Every change is recorded for the plugin to drain."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Step-4-Build-the-coordinator-and-register-the-plugin","text":"Step 4: Build the coordinator and register the plugin","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", build a local container, create a "},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", register its plugin, and run first-load hydration before constructing the store:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured() async -> AppStore {","        let container = try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","","        let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","            entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","            container: container,","            debounce: .milliseconds(250)","        )","","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","        \/\/ Register UndoPlugin first if you use it — snapshots must precede writes.","        plugins.register(persistence.corePlugin)","","        var initial = AppState()","        await persistence.hydrate(into: &initial)   \/\/ first-load: fill EntityStores from disk","","        return Store(initialState: initial, reducer: { … }, plugins: plugins)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"hydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first-load only","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — it replaces each ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" with the on-disk rows before any live edits exist. It takes ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" because it runs ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before the store is built"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", so there is nothing to race with.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The only refresh path after launch is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rehydrate(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"reconciles","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rather than replaces: rows on disk are authoritative except for IDs that still carry unflushed local intent, which always win. So a “refresh from disk” can never clobber pending writes or in-progress UI edits, while remote edits and deletions still surface mid-session. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"policy:"},{"type":"text","text":" — or register an entity with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"policy:"},{"type":"text","text":" — to narrow that; see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MergePolicy"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It takes the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"store","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": re-hydration is asynchronous, and a caller holding a state snapshot across those "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":"s would discard everything dispatched while they were in flight. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"},{"type":"text","text":" if edits are vanishing after a load."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need to "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"read"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" rows without touching state, don’t re-hydrate into a throwaway "},{"code":"AppState()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — that idiom breaks silently the moment re-hydration starts reading the state it is handed. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetchAll(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"snapshot(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on the coordinator instead."}]},{"anchor":"Reading-rows-without-touching-state","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Reading rows without touching state"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For exports, migrations, diagnostics, or any other “what’s actually on disk?” question, read directly — naming your domain type, not its generated shadow:"}]},{"code":["let notes = try await persistence.fetchAll(of: Note.self)","let store = try await persistence.snapshot(of: Note.self)   \/\/ as an EntityStore"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both flush the debounce window first by default, so they can’t return a stale row for something the user just edited; pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"flushPending: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a hot path where that doesn’t matter. Both report failures to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFailure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" rethrow — there is no state to leave untouched here, so swallowing the error could only present an unreadable database as “no data”.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The entity does not have to be registered with the coordinator; reading a model that is in the container’s schema but not mirrored into state is fine.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Don’t answer these questions by re-hydrating into a throwaway "},{"code":"AppState()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". That reads like a pure fetch but is really a merge, and it breaks silently the moment re-hydration starts consulting the state it is handed."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Surfacing failures","anchor":"Surfacing-failures"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every save and fetch failure is logged, and the coordinator accepts an optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFailure:"},{"text":" handler to additionally surface it to your app (a failed ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"save","type":"text"}]},{"text":" means the in-memory data is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" on disk; a failed ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hydrate fetch"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves that "},{"code":"EntityStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" untouched rather than presenting an unreadable store as “no data”):","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","    container: container,","    onFailure: { failure in","        guard failure.isFinal else { return }   \/\/ earlier attempts may still succeed","        \/\/ e.g. dispatch an action that shows a \"couldn't save\" banner","    }",")"]},{"text":"Retrying a failed save","type":"heading","anchor":"Retrying-a-failed-save","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A flush clears its buffers before the save runs, so a save that fails has nothing left to retry it — the write would reach disk only if the user happened to touch the same entity again. That is silent data loss, so the stack retries.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A failed batch goes ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"back"}]},{"type":"text","text":" into the writer’s pending buffers, never over anything newer: a later edit to the same entity supersedes the restored value, and a deletion drained while the save was in flight cancels it. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" then re-attempts on a doubling backoff, independently of the debounce timer — a write has to land even if the user never touches the app again."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Retrying is bounded, because a write that can "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"never","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" succeed (disk full, a model the container can’t encode) must not keep the stack busy forever. Tune it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"retry:"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","    container: container,","    retry: RetryPolicy(maxAttempts: 5, baseDelay: .milliseconds(500), maxDelay: .seconds(30)),","    onFailure: { failure in ... }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RetryPolicy.default"},{"type":"text","text":" is that policy — five attempts over roughly seven seconds. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RetryPolicy.never"},{"type":"text","text":" opts out of retrying without opting back into losing the write."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the budget runs out you get one final "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceFailure"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isFinal == true"},{"type":"text","text":". That is the one worth telling the user about: everything before it was “we’ll try again”. The batch is "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" discarded — it stays pending, so the next edit or an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" tries once more, and until then those IDs stay locally owned so a re-hydration can’t overwrite them with the stale stored row."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every attempt is reported, so a handler that shows UI should gate on ","type":"text"},{"code":"isFinal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Most ","type":"text"},{"code":".save","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" failures are transient and are followed by a success the app never hears about.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Diagnostics: what isn’t a failure","anchor":"Diagnostics-what-isnt-a-failure"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some conditions are worth acting on but aren’t errors, so routing them through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFailure"},{"type":"text","text":" would be wrong. Duplicate rows are the clearest case: CloudKit forbids unique constraints, so several rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" are a legitimate on-disk state, not a fault. They go to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDiagnostic:"},{"type":"text","text":" instead:"}]},{"code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards, collapse: EntityCollapse.byID { $0.updatedAt >= $1.updatedAt ? $0 : $1 })],","    container: container,","    onDiagnostic: { diagnostic in","        guard diagnostic.kind == .duplicateRowsCollapsed,","              let count = diagnostic.duplicateCount else { return }","        store.send(.offerDuplicateCleanup(count: count))","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three kinds ship today:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Kind","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Means"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Payload","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".duplicateRowsCollapsed"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A read found rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Without a ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" resolver they are harmless but permanent — this is what lets you ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"offer"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the cleanup.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"entityType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"duplicateCount","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".possibleDispatchLoop"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" fired far more often in one debounce interval than a user could cause. Usually an effect or plugin dispatching on every state change. Reported once per burst, not once per dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drainCount"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".writesUnpersisted"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The set of IDs whose last flush failed changed. Fires again with an ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"empty","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" set once they land, so an indicator can be cleared rather than guessed at.","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"entityType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"unpersistedIDs","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"PersistenceDiagnostic","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a struct with static constructors rather than an enum, so a future kind can’t break an exhaustive "},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in your code — match on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"type":"text","text":" and read the payload you expect. Duplicate reads and dispatch loops are logged whether or not you supply a handler; the unpersisted set has no log of its own, because the individual "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceFailure"},{"type":"text","text":"s behind it are already logged."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 5: Flush on background","anchor":"Step-5-Flush-on-background"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writes are debounced, so drain them when the app is backgrounded or terminates:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await persistence.corePlugin.flush() }","    }","}"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Multiple entities and ordering","anchor":"Multiple-entities-and-ordering"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register one "},{"code":".entity(\\.keyPath)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.decks), .entity(\\.cards), .entity(\\.tags)],","    container: try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(","        models: [DeckModel.self, CardModel.self, TagModel.self]","    )",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass every generated ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"…Model"},{"text":" type to the container’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"models:"},{"text":". Writers flush in registration order — if entity B holds a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation"},{"type":"text","text":" to A, register A’s entity first."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Testing","anchor":"Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The whole stack runs against an in-memory SwiftData store, so persistence is unit-testable with no disk and no CloudKit:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let container = try ContainerFactory.makeInMemoryContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","let db = EntityDB(modelContainer: container)","","try await db.upsert(Card(id: id, quote: \"hi\", createdAt: .now), as: CardModel.self)","let all = try await db.fetchAll(CardModel.self)","#expect(all.first?.quote == \"hi\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To prove the rule-#8 merge guarantee, seed the store, make a live in-memory edit, call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coordinator.rehydrate(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and assert the live edit survives."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/How